@format 1
@id processing.complete
@title Complete processing
@area 5. Processing and FFmpeg
@entry input
@summary Commit a finished job as done or failed, reload observable state, apply failure-pausing policy, and clean temporary resources.
@section II. Functionality
@flow TB
@related processing.run-job, relay.deliver-output
@tag processing
@tag completion

@alias job = Cadroue.ShellEngine.LJob
@alias schedule = Cadroue.Infrastructure.LSchedule
@alias runner = Cadroue.ShellEngine.LRunner

[input] Job reaches a final result <input>
- Receive final FFmpeg status and collected output metadata @ job.LJobRun(...)
> commit

[commit] Commit final state <decision>
- Set finish time, sizes, media metadata, progress, state, and message @ job.LJobRun(...)
- Move the running record to done or failed storage @ schedule.LScheduleCommit(...)
- Save final record details and reload the schedule @ schedule.LScheduleCommit(...)
? "Job succeeded" > done
? "Job failed" > failed

[done] Successful result <process>
= Output metadata is visible and the durable work record is done.
> cleanup

[failed] Failed result <process>
- Pause the queue when failure-pausing is enabled @ runner.LRunnerFailureApply(...)
> cleanup

[cleanup] Release job resources <output>
- Remove process and live-item registrations and stop lease renewal @ job.LJobRun(...) / finally
- Remove temporary stage files @ job.LJobTempClear(...)
= Job-owned runtime resources are released; the durable record remains done or failed.
